{"authority":"Riley ruling 2026-11-23 22:53 CST: Tasha's and Riley's specified teams are their starting teams and scale as they grow, both when played as the protagonist and when encountered in the story.","design_constants":{"constant_status":"LABELED DESIGN CONSTANTS (project design-constant precedent, cf. styler_params.gd). The curve is anchored on the verified evolution thresholds so first evolutions land across beats 2-3 and final evolutions across beats 4-6; it is tunable at bind time without touching any verified team data.","encountered_beat_levels":{"0":7,"1":16,"2":24,"3":32,"4":40,"5":48,"6":56,"7":64,"8":72,"postgame":87},"encountered_offset":2,"evolution_state_rule":"At any beat, a level-evolution member's stage is the highest stage whose verified level threshold is <= the beat level. A member AT its threshold level has evolved (threshold is inclusive).","item_evolution_rule":"ITEM-EVO RULE: an item-evolution member evolves at the first beat by which every level-evolution teammate has completed its FIRST evolution (the team's First Evolution Round). On this curve that is beat 3 for both teams. The required item is treated as in the protagonist's possession from that beat (played variant) and as applied at that beat (encountered variant). Item evolution is beat-keyed, not level-keyed, in both variants. Reason: parity - no member is left a stage behind its teammates, and neither Heliolisk nor Appletun is stranded unevolved into the late game waiting on an item the scaling table cannot schedule.","played_beat_levels":{"0":5,"1":14,"2":22,"3":30,"4":38,"5":46,"6":54,"7":62,"8":70,"postgame":85}},"endgame_note":"Level-100 endgame contexts (Final World Coronation, Leon as 101st challenger) sit outside the badge-beat system. If a protagonist team is fielded there, it uses its postgame row's final stages at the encounter's own level standard (100); no separate table is authored here because the beat system the ruling names ends at post-game.","eviolite_note":"e